Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" --deselect tests/units/api/test_routes.py::TestHealthRoutes::test_readiness_route_returns_checks`
-> 9754 passed, 338 skipped, 9 deselected, 22 warnings in 36.33s.
The deselected readiness test opens a real SQL warehouse session against the
conftest's fake host and hangs in connector retries on networks where that
host doesn't fail fast; it is unrelated to this change.
Local smoke run (REGISTRY_BACKEND=sqlite, no Lakebase): app boots, readiness
reports "SQLite registry ready", domain create / save / list / version /
edit lock / load round trip through the HTTP API works, and new domains get
the Lakehouse graph backend.
